load @term/seed/code/space/topological
  find topological-space

# A sheaf: an assignment of data to each open set of a space, consistent under restriction, so that local data agreeing
# on overlaps glues to global data. It is the tool for tracking how local information (functions, sections, solutions)
# patches together over a space. A presheaf is the assignment without the gluing law; a sheaf adds it. The form carries
# the underlying topological space; the restriction maps and the gluing axiom are the structure.
form sheaf
  link space, like topological-space
